module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.GameBlocks

/-!
# The finite game in bit masks: 97 blocks of period 15 and 16

The finite game of [`FiniteGame`](FiniteGame.md), run on every primitive block of period at most 16, excludes 197
blocks, 136 of them beyond the kit. `GameBlocks` checks 32 of those of period at most 14 in the kernel; this module
checks 97 of the 102 of period 15 and 16, those whose game needs at most 9 cells, with the same certificates
(`GameMask.check`) and the same theorem (`mask_column`). The other five need games of 12 to 14 cells.

`center_not_gameBlocks16` excludes each of the 97 blocks as the eventual period of the center column, from any time on
and in any rotation, and `not_eventually_gameBlocks16` states the same in the kit's form
`Rule30StripCertificates.EventuallyWord`.

The natural-language argument is `GameBlocksLong.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata
open Rule30StripCertificateTable (wordOf)

